Scope of this license
---------------------

This repository combines parts with different provenance.

1. Dual-boot / recovery source

   The boot manager sketches (ats-mini-recovery-beta, ats-mini-recovery-lite),
   the partition tables, and the flashing/build scripts (for example
   ats-mini-recovery-lite/flash-lite.ps1) are provided under this MIT License.
   Display.h descends from the upstream ATS Mini project, which is MIT
   licensed, Copyright (c) 2025 ESP32-SI4732 Radio (see NOTICE section 2).

2. Bootloader binaries (not covered by this MIT License)

   ats-mini-recovery-beta/bootloader.bin and ats-mini-recovery-lite/bootloader.bin
   are modified ESP-IDF builds. ESP-IDF is distributed by Espressif under the
   Apache License 2.0, so these binaries are covered by Apache-2.0, not by this
   MIT License. See NOTICE section 3.1 and LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

Third-party components
----------------------

Files and materials that carry a different copyright or license notice are not
relicensed under this MIT License. In particular, Rotary.cpp and Rotary.h are
Copyright 2011 Ben Buxton and licensed under GPL-3.0 (see
LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt). The Arduino-ESP32 core and the other libraries linked
into the firmware images are covered by their own terms (LGPL-2.1-or-later
and others; see NOTICE and LICENSES/LGPL-2.1.txt). Other third-party
components remain subject to their own license terms; see the NOTICE file and
the LICENSES directory.

Firmware binaries
-----------------

Firmware releases from this repository contain code under more than one
license. Each part keeps its own terms:

- The application images built from ats-mini-recovery-beta and
  ats-mini-recovery-lite link Rotary.cpp and Rotary.h, which are GPL-3.0
  (see the NOTICE file). Distributing such an image distributes GPL-3.0
  covered code: keep the copyright notices and the license text, state
  that the work was modified where the applicable license requires it, and
  provide the corresponding source code (this repository at the matching
  commit or tag).
- The bootloader binaries are Apache-2.0, not MIT (see above).
- The Arduino-ESP32 core and the other libraries linked into the images
  keep their own license terms; see NOTICE sections 3, 4 and 5.

Sending an application image to a device over OTA is binary distribution
as well, and carries the same obligations as any other release download.

This MIT License does not cover the combined firmware images.
